From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:44:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_TOPK, route K of the
 model's 10 experts per token (default off)

Routes the top K of the model's 10 experts per token. Unset, routing is the model's own 10 experts and the engine is
unchanged.

Idea: azampatti's 5-expert INT4-AutoRound checkpoint, https://huggingface.co/azampatti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-125B-A5B-INT4-AutoRound

Changes, in the order they were made:
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_TOPK, route K of the model's 10 experts per token (default off)

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_TOPK is off unset, 0 or the model's own 10, takes 1-9 and refuses anything else
